<title>USA: Florsheim to sell Chicago headquarters.</title>
<headline>Florsheim to sell Chicago headquarters.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florsheim Shoe Co said Thursday it signed a contract to sell its downtown Chicago headquarters building to Everest Partners LLC for $8.1 million cash.</p>
<p>The shoemaker also said it signed a long-term corporate headquarters lease at 200 North LaSalle St., another downtown Chicago location. That 12-year-old building is owned by Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association of America.</p>
<p>Florsheim said the move would allow it to reduce its occupancy costs. It expects to close on the sale of its building by the end of the year.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk, 312 408-8787</p>
